    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>Pacifism covers a spectrum from the belief that international disputes can and should be settled peacefully to opposition to violence under any circumstance, even in defence of self and others.</li><li>Its organised form dates from 1815 and 1816, when the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a> Peace Society and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a> Peace Society were founded, and it drew on two strands of thought: the secular <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/age-of-enlightenment">Enlightenment</a> and the evangelical religious revival.</li><li><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahatma-gandhi">Mahatma Gandhi</a>'s satyagraha served as inspiration to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/martin-luther-king-jr">Martin Luther King Jr.</a> and many others in the civil rights movement, while critics from Hitler to Orwell to Jan Narveson attacked pacifism on very different grounds.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>On 1 December 1948 President <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jose-figueres-ferrer">José Figueres Ferrer</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/costa-rica">Costa Rica</a> abolished the Costa Rican military, and in 1949 the abolition was introduced in Article 12 of the constitution.</p></aside>
    </section>

